From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ThaRae <76752281+ThaRae@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:44:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: Drop owed hover events once a newer mouse event is
 handled

A rendering update can note the boundary events a resting pointer is
owed, at the position the lanes last saw it. The host should take them
only if it handled no mouse move since, and request_hover() drops them
when the host hovers a move's target itself. But a move the host hands
to a same-process iframe never reaches request_hover() on the parent's
host. So the parent took the owed events after that move, at the
pointer's old position, and told the iframe that the pointer had left,
which ended the link hover the move had just reported.

Drop the owed events when the host notes a newer mouse event as
handled. This made TestLinkHoverStatus fail now and then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Libraries/LibWeb/Rust/src/render_state/document_host.rs | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/Rust/src/render_state/document_host.rs b/Libraries/LibWeb/Rust/src/render_state/document_host.rs
index a46d9d2b82f036b70ae6eeae8434c29b8438ca3a..bf2080966161b51ff9dec13018cc265be084f6a2 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/Rust/src/render_state/document_host.rs
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/Rust/src/render_state/document_host.rs
@@ -991,6 +991,9 @@ impl DocumentHost {
         if input_event_id < self.newest_pointer_input_event.get() {
             return true;
         }
+        if input_event_id > self.newest_pointer_input_event.get() {
+            self.hover_events_owed.set(None);
+        }
         self.newest_pointer_input_event.set(input_event_id);
         // NB: Lanes may tick beside a task that handles a press, and no tick hovers a move older than this event.
         self.ticks.note_input_handled(input_event_id);
